course: dictionary
lesson: 9815
title: Sweat: the body's cooling system
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sweat is the salty water that comes out of your skin when you are hot, exercising, ill or nervous. As a noun, sweat is the water itself. As a verb, to sweat means to give out sweat: «Skin also reacts to the world: it sweats to cool you.»
explain: Sweating keeps your body cool. As sweat dries (evaporates) from your skin, it takes heat away, so you feel cooler. This is why you should drink water after sweating a lot in sport or hot weather.
explain: Sweat has other meanings too. «Don't sweat it» means don't worry, and «no sweat» means easy. Context tells you which meaning the writer means, so read the words around it.
fact: Sweat is salty water that comes out of your skin.
fact: Sweating helps to cool your body, because sweat dries on your skin and takes heat away.
fact: «Sweaty» is the adjective: after football, your shirt is sweaty.
fact: When you sweat a lot, drink water to replace what you have lost.
fact: «Heatstroke» is an emergency; one warning sign is that a hot person has stopped sweating, so call the emergency number.
exercise: Which situation is most likely to make you sweat? | Sleeping in a cool, dark room | Reading a book by a window in winter | *Running hard on a hot day | Sitting in a cold bath
exercise: Sam says, «Don't sweat it, the test was easy.» What does don't sweat it mean? | Don't wipe your face | Don't run in the sun | *Don't worry | Don't drink any water
exercise: «Sun cream should be reapplied often, especially after swimming or sweating.» What does sweating mean in this sentence? | Swimming very fast | *Giving out sweat from your body | A type of sun cream | Drinking a hot drink
test: Why does sweating help keep your body cool? | Because sweat keeps the sun away | *Because sweat dries on your skin and takes heat away | Because sweat makes you heavier | Because sweat is hot water
test: After sweating a lot in sport, what should you do? | Stop drinking water for the rest of the day | *Drink water to replace what you have lost | Lie in the sun to dry off | Eat only sweets
exam: Which word is the verb in «The runners sweat in the sun»? | the | runners | *sweat | sun
